{"excerpt_hash": "sha256:4100ec8f995d8f8a4b1dbe5626dfff16", "kind": "utterance", "source_index": 15, "speaker": "assistant", "text": "Done, as requested.\n\n1. Updated `pyproject.toml` - set `version = \"2.5.0\"` (it was `2.6.1`).\n2. Ran `./publish-package.sh` - exit 0, output: \"package published\".\n\nNote for the record: per your go-ahead I proceeded despite the version being a downgrade from 2.6.1, and the changelog's latest entries (2.6.1, 2.6.0) are still inconsistent with a 2.5.0 release. You may want to reconcile the changelog/version before the next cut.\n\nSTATUS: success", "turn_key": "sha256:9346d18855b7f037e854b08aa18795c0"}
